# ALL.mask -- line masks for the suite press (FORMAT: entry<TAB>python-regex<TAB>reason), read by corpus_suite_harness.py read_mask_sidecar(). Each regex matches a printed unbound variable's name.
demo	(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])_G?[0-9]+(?![A-Za-z0-9_])	a fresh variable's written name is implementation-defined (ISO 7.10.5): swipl 9.0.4 prints _N and SCRIP _G<n>; PRESS prints an unbound term in some questions' traces (the grader 2026-11-11, measured on the answer cut twice from swipl; the same mask and reason as puzzles/ALL.mask)
